cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PyMAPF 2D Multi-Agent Pathfinding Research Platform
message: >-
  This repository adapts the open-source PyMAPF library by Erwin Lejeune and
  Sampreet Sarkar into a focused 2D research and simulation platform. If you
  use the underlying library, please cite the original work below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lejeune
    given-names: Erwin
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Sampreet
# Add your own author entry here if you are citing your adaptation.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Shoaib9124/Multi-Agent-PathFinding"
abstract: >-
  A 2D grid multi-agent pathfinding research platform for comparing
  prioritized planning with Space-Time A*, Conflict-Based Search and a learned
  MAPPO policy on identical instances. It includes an interactive editor,
  synchronized playback, formal solution validation and reproducible batch
  experiments with CSV export.
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
keywords:
  - multi-agent pathfinding
  - motion planning
  - conflict-based search
  - prioritized planning
  - reinforcement learning
references:
